/*!

@page Player


__Player__ :

Following are the major features supported by QMMF-SDK Player:
- MP4 playback: \n
  a. Video : Supports H264, H265 video formats \n
  b. Audio : Supports AAC, AMR, G711 audio formats
- Trick modes: \n
  a. Slow forward: 1/2x, 1/4x, 1/8x \n
  b. Fast forward: 2x, 4x, 8x \n
  c. Rewind
- Seek(Set Position) and Drag
- Capture image when pause or stop


@tableofcontents
______

@section Player_Diagrams Player Class Diagram

@image html /Images/player_class_diagram.png
\n
______

@section Buffer_Allocation_and_Management Buffer Allocation and Management

@subsection Video Video

- The player allocates buffers based on the requirements it gets from AVCodec module.  On the input side (to AVCodec), 4 buffers are allocated and on the output side, 9 buffers are allocated.

\code{.cpp}
avcodec_->GetBufferRequirements(Port,  &count, &size);
\endcode

The count variable fetches the number of buffers to be allocated based on the port while size stores the size of each buffer to be allocated.

- We maintain the following queues for each port,
  On the input port, we have:
  1. input_buffer_list: Contains all the input buffers allocated by player.
  2. unfilled_frame_queue: Contains all the buffers which the application can Dequeue to fill encoded data.
  3. filled_frame_queue: Contains all the buffers which are filled by the application and given to player.
  4. frames_to_decode_: The video encoded frames to be given to Video decoder
  5. frames_being_decoded_: The video encoded frames given to the avcodec.

  All the input port related handling can be found in qmmf_player_video_decoder_core.cc file

  On the output port, we have:
  1. output_buffer_list_: Contains all the output buffers allocated by player.
  2. output_free_buffer_queue_: The empty buffers given to AVCodec to fill the decoded data.
  3. output_occupy_buffer_queue_: The Video decoded frames we get from AVCodec.
  4. decoded_buffer_queue_: The Video decoded frames we get from AVCodec and to be given to display

  All the output port/display related handling can be found in qmmf_player_video_decoder_core.cc file

@image html /Images/player_video_buffer_management.png
\n
______

@section AV_Sync AV Sync

AV Sync in player is achieved by keeping Audio free running and adjusting the displayed frames based on difference of timestamps for audio and video.

@image html /Images/player_av_sync.png
\n
______

@section Debug_Knobs Debug Knobs

Info and error logs are enabled by default which give minimal information regarding the workflow.
\n
To enable more logs, set the property mentioned below and restart the qmmf-server or reboot the device for changes to take effect
\n
<b> adb shell setprop persist.qmmf.sdk.log.level "value" </b>
where value is, \n
0, none of the debug/verbose logs are enabled.\n
1, Debug logs are enabled.\n
2, Both Debug and Verbose Logs are enabled.
______

